  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Mosiah",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 24,
    "summary": "Amulon persecutes Alma and his people—They are to be put to death if they pray—The Lord makes their burdens seem light—He delivers them from bondage, and they return to Zarahemla. About 145–120 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Amulon did gain favor in the eyes of the king of the Lamanites; therefore, the king of the Lamanites granted unto him and his brethren that they should be appointed teachers over his people, yea, even over the people who were in the land of Shemlon, and in the land of Shilom, and in the land of Amulon.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 313,
            "end": 327,
            "text": "Mosiah 23:31; Alma 21:3 (2–4)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:1",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "For the Lamanites had taken possession of all these lands; therefore, the king of the Lamanites had appointed kings over all these lands.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:2",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And now the name of the king of the Lamanites was Laman, being called after the name of his father; and therefore he was called king Laman. And he was king over a numerous people.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Mosiah 9:10 (10–11); 10:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:3",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And he appointed teachers of the brethren of Amulon in every land which was possessed by his people; and thus the language of Nephi began to be taught among all the people of the Lamanites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "Mosiah 2:4; 18:18 (18–22); 23:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Mosiah 23:9 (9, 12, 31)."
          },
          {
            "start": 114,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "Omni 1:18."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Omni 1:18.",
            "prettyString": "Omni 1:18",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "omni",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 1,
                    "end": 1,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 18,
                        "end": 18
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:4",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And they were a people friendly one with another; nevertheless they knew not God; neither did the brethren of Amulon teach them anything concerning the Lord their God, neither the law of Moses; nor did they teach them the words of Abinadi;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:5",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "But they taught them that they should keep their record, and that they might write one to another.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:6",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus the Lamanites began to increase in riches, and began to trade one with another and wax great, and began to be a cunning and a wise people, as to the wisdom of the world, yea, a very cunning people, delighting in all manner of wickedness and plunder, except it were among their own brethren.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "Gen. 34:10 (10–21); 4 Ne. 1:46."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:7",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And now it came to pass that Amulon began to exercise authority over Alma and his brethren, and began to persecute him, and cause that his children should persecute their children.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Mosiah 23:32."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "D&C 121:39."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Mosiah 23:32.",
            "prettyString": "Mosiah 23:32",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "mosiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 23,
                    "end": 23,
                    "verses": [
