                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:8",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "For Amulon knew Alma, that he had been one of the king’s priests, and that it was he that believed the words of Abinadi and was driven out before the king, and therefore he was wroth with him; for he was subject to king Laman, yet he exercised authority over them, and put tasks upon them, and put task-masters over them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Mosiah 17:2 (1–4); 23:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 273,
            "end": 278,
            "text": "Mosiah 21:3 (3–6)."
          },
          {
            "start": 298,
            "end": 310,
            "text": "Mosiah 23:37 (37–39)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:9",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that so great were their afflictions that they began to cry mightily to God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:10",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And Amulon commanded them that they should stop their cries; and he put guards over them to watch them, that whosoever should be found calling upon God should be put to death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 71,
            "text": "Dan. 6:7 (7–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mosiah 24:11",
        "book": "Mosiah",
        "chapter": 24,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And Alma and his people did not raise their voices to the Lord their God, but did pour out their hearts to him; and he did know the thoughts of their hearts.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "TG Prayer."
          },
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 140,
            "text": "Ps. 139:2; Matt. 12:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
